{
  "_comment": [
    "Dataset panel for the expanded memorization screening.",
    "prepare_datasets.py downloads each source and writes data/screening/<key>.csv with the",
    "canonical schema: mol_id, smiles, value  (+ smiles_random, smiles_blind, value_blind).",
    "",
    "class: 'measured'  = experimental values, the contamination-prone kind (one iconic file on the web)",
    "       'computed'  = values produced by a calculation, typically distributed as an archive not a lookup table",
    "       'neg_control' = published after every audited model's training cutoff",
    "       'pos_control' = values the models demonstrably know (calibrates the detector's ceiling)",
    "",
    "prompt_property / prompt_unit / prompt_dsname are interpolated into the zero-shot prompt by",
    "Run_ZeroShot.jl. Keeping them here (not in code) is what makes adding a dataset a data-only change.",
    "",
    "decimals_hint: typical number of significant figures in the published values. Datasets whose",
    "values carry <3 significant figures cannot support the 3-sig test and are scored at 2-sig only."
  ],
  "datasets": [
